Overview

Built a virtualization lab environment to safely test multiple operating systems, learn system administration basics, and practice using isolated environments without affecting the main computer.

Components

Virtualization Software | VirtualBox
Host System            | Personal Desktop PC
Guest OS 1             | Kali Linux
Guest OS 2             | Windows 11
Resources              | Virtual CPU, RAM, Storage
Networking             | Virtual Network Adapters

Process

Installed VirtualBox on the host system and created multiple virtual machines for different use cases. Allocated CPU cores, memory, and storage based on each operating system’s needs. Installed Kali Linux and Windows 11 as guest systems. Configured virtual networking and basic settings for usability. Used the virtual machines for learning, testing software, and practicing OS installation without risking the host machine.

Skills Learned

* Virtualization fundamentals
* VM creation and management
* Operating system installation
* Resource allocation planning
* Virtual networking basics
* Safe testing environments
* Multi-OS administration
* Snapshot/recovery awareness
